     - <h3>5A Water Clock</h3>
     - <p>A water clock, also known as a clepsydra, is a device that measures time by the flow of water. It works by 
     - <ul>
     - <li>Outflow: Water flows out of a container, and the time is measured by how much water has left.</li>
     - <li>Inflow: Water flows into a container, and the time is measured by how much water has entered.</li>
     - </ul>
     - <img class="img-fluid" loading="lazy" src="https://placehold.co/800x450?text=image" alt="" />
